From: Tiberiu Chibici <chibicitiberiu@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 12:39:03 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 11/11] AcceleratedSurface: shared-memory frames in Cairo's
 byte order on big-endian

In the shared-memory mode the web process reads each composited frame back with glReadPixels(GL_BGRA, GL_UNSIGNED_BYTE), the bytes B, G, R, A, and the UI process wraps the buffer as CAIRO_FORMAT_ARGB32, a native-endian word: A, R, G, B in memory on big-endian. On big-endian each pixel's bytes are now reversed after the read.
---
 .../WebPage/CoordinatedGraphics/AcceleratedSurface.cpp   | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Source/WebKit/WebProcess/WebPage/CoordinatedGraphics/AcceleratedSurface.cpp b/Source/WebKit/WebProcess/WebPage/CoordinatedGraphics/AcceleratedSurface.cpp
index fc00aa6..95297b3 100644
--- a/Source/WebKit/WebProcess/WebPage/CoordinatedGraphics/AcceleratedSurface.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebKit/WebProcess/WebPage/CoordinatedGraphics/AcceleratedSurface.cpp
@@ -514,6 +514,15 @@ AcceleratedSurface::RenderTargetSHMImage::~RenderTargetSHMImage()
 void AcceleratedSurface::RenderTargetSHMImage::didRenderFrame(Vector<IntRect, 1>&& damageRects)
 {
     glReadPixels(0, 0, m_bitmap->size().width(), m_bitmap->size().height(), GL_BGRA, GL_UNSIGNED_BYTE, m_bitmap->mutableSpan().data());
+#if CPU(BIG_ENDIAN)
+    // GL_BGRA gives the bytes B, G, R, A; the UI process takes the buffer as Cairo's ARGB32, a
+    // native-endian word: the bytes A, R, G, B on big-endian.
+    auto pixels = m_bitmap->mutableSpan();
+    for (size_t i = 0; i + 4 <= pixels.size(); i += 4) {
+        std::swap(pixels[i], pixels[i + 3]);
+        std::swap(pixels[i + 1], pixels[i + 2]);
+    }
+#endif
     RenderTargetShareableBuffer::didRenderFrame(WTF::move(damageRects));
 }
 
